---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleCard from "../../components/ArticleCard.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles"))
  .filter((article) => article.data.category === "Global Food Crisis")
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---

<BaseLayout title="Global Food Crisis | Food Supply Crisis Report" description="Evidence-based reporting on global food crises, hunger hotspots, food insecurity, price shocks and food-supply risks.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Topic Hub</p><h1>Global Food Crisis</h1><p>Understand the difference between global availability, regional shortages, high prices and acute food insecurity.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Read the global picture without losing regional detail</h2>
      <p>A global food-crisis assessment needs more than one headline statistic. Total production describes how much food is being produced; trade and stocks describe how supplies move and what buffers exist; price data describes market pressure; humanitarian assessments describe whether people can obtain enough food.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Availability</h3><p>Check crop production, ending stocks, exports and import capacity. FAO's <a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cereal Supply and Demand Brief</a> tracks the global cereal balance.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Affordability</h3><p>Use the <a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/foodpricesindex/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAO Food Price Index</a> for international commodity movements, then compare local consumer-price data and income conditions.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Acute hunger</h3><p>For severe regional food insecurity, use current <a href="https://www.ipcinfo.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPC analyses</a> and <a href="https://www.wfp.org/publications" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WFP assessments</a> rather than inferring hunger from global prices.</p></article>
      </div>
      <h3>October 2026 baseline</h3>
      <p>In its 2 October update, FAO forecast global cereal output at 2.979 billion tonnes for 2026. That is 2.1% below the previous year's record but still the second-largest harvest on record. At the same time, FAO projected lower cereal trade amid constrained Black Sea shipping. This mixed picture is why high global output does not rule out local access crises or upward price pressure.</p>
      <p><a href="/articles/food-collapse-fact-check-2026/">See how to test a global food-collapse claim</a> or read the <a href="/articles/global-food-crisis-2026/">full 2026 assessment</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="card-grid">
    {articles.map((article) => <ArticleCard article={article} />)}
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
